From fc1c77144b94eb5648c4bc05702f7b38952e7e10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthieu Requenna | MonsieurNours <matthieu.requenna@live.fr>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:26:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kycontroller: add POST /force_idr

A client whose decoder lost a reference picture (packets lost beyond
what the FEC repairs) has no way to recover quickly: with intra refresh,
the default, the encoder never sends a keyframe on its own. Some
decoders (VLC) go on with a damaged picture that heals itself over the
refresh period; others (VideoToolbox) reject every following frame and
the picture stays frozen.

Add POST /force_idr, with the same authentication and scope as
/set_bitrate: it forces a keyframe on the video streams of the session
that asks, with the mechanism already used when a relay lags behind.
Requests are rate-limited per session: within 150 ms of the last forced
keyframe, a request is ignored (still answered 200, the keyframe is on
its way) and logged at debug level. Without the limit, a client losing
packets continuously would get a keyframe per round trip, and every
client of a shared stream would pay for them.
---
 kycontroller/src/controller.rs |  3 ++
 kycontroller/src/main.rs       | 73 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 74 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

